# .worktreeinclude - gitignored paths Orca copies into each new local worktree.
# Docs: https://www.onorca.dev/docs/model/orca-yaml
#
# One literal path per line. No globs, no negation. Entries must exist and be
# gitignored in the primary checkout; missing entries are skipped silently.
# Copies are private per worktree - changing a value in the primary checkout
# does not propagate to existing worktrees.
#
# A fresh worktree has no data otherwise: data/ contains only the gitignored
# raw/ directory, and nba.duckdb is gitignored too. There is no network fetch in
# the pipeline, so raw/ is the only source of truth.
#
# .bruin.yml holds the duckdb connection paths (relative, no secrets) and is
# required for bruin to resolve connections at all.
#
# nba.duckdb is 420 MB. Copying it costs seconds on ext4 and skips a full
# `make run` rebuild; drop it from this list if worktree disk usage matters more.

.bruin.yml
nba.duckdb
data/raw
